--TEST--
`spawn script` reports the parent's own mistakes as throws rather than as a `ScriptResult` — ADR 0006 § *Decision*, § *Failure is a value, not an exception*
--FILE--
<?nvs
// ADR 0006's failure-is-a-value rule is about what the *child* did. A path
// that names nothing and an `output:` spelling that is neither of the two the
// ADR gives were both written by the parent before any child existed, so they
// are ordinary throws here — `crates/nvs-runtime/src/script.rs`'s module doc
// is the one home of "this is one step before the boundary".
try {
    spawn script "no-such-child.nvs";
    echo "unreachable", "\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $missing) {
    echo $missing->message, "\n";
}

// The other option spelling. Refused rather than defaulted, because a
// misspelled `'inherait'` would otherwise silently capture.
try {
    spawn script "no-such-child.nvs" with(output: "inherait");
    echo "unreachable", "\n";
} catch (LogicError $bad) {
    echo $bad->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
`spawn script 'no-such-child.nvs'`: `no-such-child.nvs` could not be compiled; see the errors above
`spawn script`'s `output:` is `'capture'` or `'inherit'`, got `'inherait'`
